# ThreadSanitizer suppressions.
#
# Empty on purpose. scripts/build-tsan.sh runs against a Qt built with
# -fsanitize=thread, so Qt's own locking is visible to TSan and the
# suppressions that the uninstrumented Qt needed (race:QMetaType,
# race:eventfd, race:QArrayData) are gone.
#
# A report entirely inside third-party code can be suppressed here, but
# only with the full stack, never by a bare function name: race:QArrayData
# was broad enough to hide a real race of ours going through a Qt
# container.
